@module render ; The animated cells: crumbling platforms, springs, bricks, fires, water, walls and the exit
@about The platform-change animations (a platform worn by the ball: 2, then 3, then 4, then gone), the spring and tilt of the platforms, the crumbling bricks, the flames and the water that puts them out, the opening locks and the turning walls. Each is a little machine stepped once a frame by MainLoop: an active flag, a step number and a table of step routines; most steps XOR the previous frame off and the next one on (DrawSpriteXor $E3EE).
$B8C2 c SetPlatformCell ; Write the new platform type of a platform-change animation into its cell
> PlatformCells $AA6B[$AB1B] = $AB20 (the cell and the new type StartWearTo3 $C3D5, StartWearTo4 $C3F8 or StartFallAway $C41B left there). Called by the first or last step of each change ($C1C3, $C1FF, $C211).
> Witness: L1 1400 (menu, l x12, rzx x91).

@module ball
$B8D1 c HitBrick ; The ball going up meets a brick: crumble a layer (a hammer for an intact brick) and send it down
> Called by the up-move handlers ($CCE9-$CE15) when the ball is under a brick cell. B = BrickContact $E1C1[BallStep]: the layer count a brick must have for the ball to touch it at this step (5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 8, 7, 6 for steps 0-7). HL = BrickLayers $AAD7 + the cell $AA44 (8 layers when the level is built, $D180); the address goes to $AA07, the count to $AA0B. No contact (count not B): return NZ.
> Contact: the screen address of the layer ($AA03 - $2002, wrapped into the CPC screen) goes to $AB31, BallState becomes 4 (down). At step 5 (an intact brick) a hammer is needed: Hammers $AAFF - 1 and the HUD ($E5E6); without one ($B952) BallStep becomes 3 and the brick is untouched. Else BallStep becomes 8 - step (the way down mirrors the way up), the crumble animation starts ($AB33 = 1, step $AB34 = 0, BrickStep $BE94), the layer count goes down by one and at 0 the cell's platform becomes 0 (the brick is gone). Witness: 369 contacts in the recordings, 47 at step 5 (each with a hammer), 46 bricks gone.
> Witness: L1 1837 (l51, l59, l96, l98, rzx x27).
$B8F3 HitBrickContact
$B903 HitBrickDown
$B921 HitBrickMirror
$B92D HitBrickMirrorSkip
$B93A HitBrickLayer
$B952 HitBrickNoHammer ; never run: no hammer, the ball just turns back

@module objects ; The objects: hammers, keys, water, bottles and prizes; the score and the exit
@about An object lies in a cell (ObjectCells $AA47, kinds 0-40). The ball takes it when it lands there: kinds 1-4 are tools and the extra life, 5 and up are prizes worth 15 points each; the last prize opens the exit.
$B958 c TakeObject ; Take the object in the ball's cell, if any
> Kind = $AB1D (ReadCell $BB32). 0: nothing. Else erases the object's sprite (ObjectSprites $6CB0 + 56 × kind, 4 bytes × 14 rows, XOR at the cell's screen address $AB2D - $9E, DrawSpriteXorInk $E3E5 with colour 7), clears ObjectCells $AA47[cell], and for kinds 1-4 jumps through ObjectHandlers $BA3D. Kinds 5 and up are prizes: the pick-up sound $F3F6 (skipped once after a long sound, $ABA7 = 4), then AddScore $BA47 with 15. Called by the landing handlers ($C811, $CA46, $CC89, $CDF9, $CEC6). Witness: 936 objects taken in the recordings, 625 prizes.
> Witness: L1 8156 (c1, fire, gameover, menu, twoname, l x12, rzx00-rzx99).
$B966 TakeObjectSprite
$B9A7 TakePrize
$B9B1 TakePrizeScore
$B9B7 TakePrizeQuiet
$B9BE c TakeNothing ; ObjectHandlers[0]: RET (kind 0 is no object, filtered out before)
> Never run: TakeObject returns on kind 0 before the jump.
> Witness: L1 0 ().
$B9BF c TakeKey ; Kind 2, a key: Keys + 1 (at most 99) and the HUD
> The pick-up sound $F3F6 unless $ABA7 = 4 (then $ABA7 = 0), Keys $AAFE + 1 unless 99, then JP $E5D3 (print the keys). Witness: 183 keys.
> Witness: L1 204 (c1, menu, l x9, rzx x60).
$B9C9 TakeKeyCount
$B9D7 TakeKeyQuiet
$B9DE c TakeWater ; Kind 3, a water drop: Water + 1 (at most 99) and the HUD
> As TakeKey with Water $AAFD and $E5C0. Witness: 54 drops.
> Witness: L1 66 (c1, gameover, menu, twoname, l x5, rzx x29).
$B9E8 TakeWaterCount
$B9F6 TakeWaterQuiet
$B9FD c TakeHammer ; Kind 1, a hammer: Hammers + 1 (at most 99) and the HUD
> As TakeKey with Hammers $AAFF and $E5E6. Witness: 58 hammers.
> Witness: L1 63 (l x5, rzx x38).
$BA07 TakeHammerCount
$BA15 TakeHammerQuiet
$BA1C c TakeBottle ; Kind 4, the bottle: an extra life
> $ABA7 = 4 (the next pick-up is silent), the sound $F40D, FirmwareStub $B747 with B = C = 26 (a dropped CPC border flash), $AB17 = 1 (BottleFlashOff undoes it next frame), lives $AB01 + 1 unless 99, then JP $E5AD (print the lives). The only way to gain a life: 15 bottles in the RZX and one in the menu recording's demo, each one life.
> Witness: L1 20 (menu, l10, l36, l45, l68, rzx x15).
$BA37 TakeBottleStore
$BA3D w ObjectHandlers 5 ; The handlers of object kinds 0-4, jumped to by TakeObject
> TakeNothing $B9BE, TakeHammer $B9FD, TakeKey $B9BF, TakeWater $B9DE, TakeBottle $BA1C.
$BA47 c AddScore ; Add BC to the score, print it, and count a prize off
> Score $AAFB += BC, PrintScore $E5A1, PrizesLeft $AA45 - 1 and OpenExit $BCB9 when it reaches 0. Only prizes come here (BC = 15).
> Witness: L1 690 (c1, menu, l x12, rzx00-rzx44, rzx46-rzx99).
$BA60 c BottleFlashOff ; The frame after a bottle: undo the border flash
> When $AB17 is set: clears it and calls FirmwareStub $B747 with B = C = 0 (a CPC border back to black; a RET here). Called by MainLoop ($ACE7) every frame.
> Witness: L1 92279 (c1, fire, gameover, menu, twoname, l x12, rzx00-rzx99).

@module hud
$BA71 c SelfDestruct ; The S key: burst the ball (in the demo, back to the main loop)
> Jumped to from the state handlers ($AE7F, $AEF6, $AF70, $AFF0, $B085, $B133) when the key $31 (S) is down. In the demo ($ABA6 not 0) it jumps back to MainLoop $ACC8 and nothing happens. With $ADDD not 0 (never: $ADDF is a RET before the store that would set it) a disabled level select runs: FirmwareStub5 $B754, then Level = L reduced below 100 by steps of 97. Then the death sound $F4CB and LoseLife.
> Witness: L1 12 (gameover, twoname).
$BA80 SelfDestructLevelSelect ; dead code
$BA84 SelfDestructReduce
$BA8C SelfDestructSetLevel
$BA90 SelfDestructSound
$BA93 c LoseLife ; The ball is lost: one life less, the level restarts (or game over, or the other player)
> Lives $AB01 = 0: GameOver $B755. Else lives - 1; Water, Keys and Hammers go back to their values at the level start ($AB06-$AB08); the 7 bytes score, water, keys, hammers, level and lives ($AAFB-$AB01) are saved in the player's record ($AB09 player 1, $AB10 player 2, by $ADDB). With two players ($ADDC = 2) the turn passes to the other player unless his record's lives byte is $FA (out): $ADDB = 1 or 2. Then 50 frames (WaitOneFrame), WaitKeyOrSecond, and JP $ABD8, which starts the level of the player whose turn it is. Entered from the burst death ($B1D1), the fall below the screen ($B2B5) and SelfDestruct. Witness: 27 runs (gameover, rzx x11): 25 lives lost, 2 game overs; the turn change is known only from the code.
> Witness: L1 34 (fire, gameover, twoname, rzx x11).
$BABE LoseLifeSave
$BADF SwitchToPlayer1
$BAE6 LoseLifePlayer1 ; player 1 was in play: is player 2 out?
$BAF1 SwitchToPlayer2
$BAF6 LoseLifeWait
$BAF8 LoseLifeWaitLoop

