@module objects ; The objects: their colours
@about The ink of each object kind, read when the level is built.
$C6F6 b ObjectInks ; The Spectrum attribute each object kind 0-40 is drawn with
> BuildLevelObject $CFF4 draws object kind K (sprite $6CB0 + 56 K, 14 lines of 4 bytes) with ink ObjectInks[K] (it patches the displacement of LD C,(IX+d) at $D01B). Kind 0 is no object and is never read. The values are attributes: $45 bright cyan, $46 bright yellow, $44 bright green, $42 bright red, $43 bright magenta, $06 yellow and so on.
@res tables/object-inks.bin

@module render
$C71F c ScreenAddrToLine ; Convert a CPC screen address to the character row, pixel line and byte column
> Input HL: an address in the CPC layout ($C000 + line in the row x $800 + row x 80 + byte). Output: ScanInRow $C74E = the line within the character row (0-7), CharRow $C74F = the row, ByteColumn $C750 = the byte column (0-79), PixelLine $C751 = row x 8 + line. Uses DivideHLbyBC $C752 for the division by 80. BC, DE, HL changed. Every picture drawn goes through it (277 064 calls in the recordings).
> Witness: L1 324616 (c1, fire, gameover, menu, twoname, l x12, rzx00-rzx99).
$C74E b ScanInRow ; The line within the character row (0-7)
$C74F CharRow ; The character row
$C750 ByteColumn ; The byte column (0-79)
$C751 PixelLine ; The pixel line, row x 8 + line
$C752 c DivideHLbyBC ; Divide HL by BC: the quotient to DivQuotient, the remainder to DivRemainder
> A 16-step shift-and-subtract division. Input HL the dividend, BC the divisor. Output HL = DivQuotient $C774, DE = DivRemainder $C776. Only ScreenAddrToLine calls it (BC = 80).
> Witness: L1 324616 (c1, fire, gameover, menu, twoname, l x12, rzx00-rzx99).
$C758 DivideStep ; one bit of the quotient a pass, 16 passes
$C763 DivideBitDone
$C774 w DivQuotient ; The quotient of the last division
$C776 DivRemainder ; The remainder

