> Witness: L1 102196 (c1, fire, gameover, menu, twoname, l x12, rzx00-rzx99).
$E61E c PrintNumber2 ; Print HL's tens and units
> PrintDigit for 10 and 1. A value of 100 or more gives a tens "digit" past 9 (the glyph after "9"); the callers pass bytes below 100 (known only from the code).
> Witness: L1 582784 (c1, fire, gameover, menu, twoname, l x12, rzx00-rzx99).
$E62B c PrintDigit ; Print HL div DE as one digit and keep HL mod DE
$E62D PrintDigitLoop
$E635 PrintDigitSkip
> Input: HL the value, DE the power of ten. C counts the subtractions; HL is left with the remainder; the glyph is Font + 8 x (C + 16) ($F649, "0"), drawn by PrintHudGlyph.
> Witness: L1 1472156 (c1, fire, gameover, menu, twoname, l x12, rzx00-rzx99).
$E639 c PrintHudGlyph ; Draw glyph C of the table at DE on the status line
> HL = DE + 8 x C, then HudBlit. HL is kept.
